# API Standards

## REST Conventions

| Action | Method | Path |
|--------|--------|------|
| List tickets | GET | `/api/tickets` |
| Create ticket | POST | `/api/tickets` |
| Get ticket | GET | `/api/tickets/{id}` |
| Update ticket | PUT | `/api/tickets/{id}` |
| Transition status | PATCH | `/api/tickets/{id}/status` |
| Add comment | POST | `/api/tickets/{id}/comments` |

Query params: `?status=OPEN&keyword=login` for filter and search.

## Request / Response

- JSON only; `Content-Type: application/json`.
- Use camelCase for JSON field names.
- Paginate list endpoints when ticket count grows (`page`, `size`, `sort`).

## Error Response Format

All 4xx/5xx responses use a consistent body:

```json
{
  "timestamp": "2026-09-18T15:30:00Z",
  "status": 400,
  "error": "Bad Request",
  "message": "Cannot transition from CLOSED to OPEN",
  "path": "/api/tickets/1/status",
  "fieldErrors": [
    { "field": "title", "message": "Title must not be blank" }
  ]
}
```

`fieldErrors` is present for validation failures; omit or empty for business-rule errors.

## HTTP Status Codes

| Code | When |
|------|------|
| 200 | Successful GET, PUT, PATCH |
| 201 | Successful POST (create) |
| 400 | Validation failure or invalid state transition |
| 404 | Ticket not found |
| 500 | Unexpected server error (log details, return generic message) |

## Versioning and Docs

- Document all endpoints in `spec/api-contract.md`.
- Expose OpenAPI/Swagger at `/swagger-ui.html` in dev profile only.
